# cREXX diagnostic message catalog, English (UK)
# Format: CODE = template with {parameter} placeholders.

ALREADY_DECLARED = Symbol is already declared.
ARGS_MISMATCH = Imported routine "{name}" has incompatible arguments between {defining_file} and {import_file}.
ARGUMENT_REQUIRED = Argument {position} ({name}) is required.
ARG_NOT_FIRST_INST = ARG must be the first instruction in a routine.
ARRAY_DIMS_MISMATCH = Array dimensions do not match.
ARRAY_ELEMENT_TYPE_MISMATCH = Array element type does not match the target type.
ASSEMBLER_ONLY_LEVELB = Inline assembler is only supported in Level B.
BAD_CONVERSION = Value cannot be converted to the required type.
BINARY_MEMORY_AT_REQUIRED = Binary memory access requires an at intrinsic.
BINARY_MEMORY_FIXED_FOR_NOT_ALLOWED = Fixed-width binary memory access must not specify a length argument.
BINARY_MEMORY_INVALID_STORAGE_TYPE = Binary memory access has an unsupported storage type.
BINARY_MEMORY_LENGTH_REQUIRED = Variable-length binary memory access requires a length argument.
BINARY_MEMORY_OFFSET_REQUIRED = Binary memory access requires a byte-position argument.
BINARY_MEMORY_READ_ONLY = Binary memory access target is read-only.
BINARY_MEMORY_SPAN_WRITE_UNSUPPORTED = Variable-length binary memory writes are not supported yet.
BINARY_MEMORY_TARGET_NOT_BINARY = Binary memory access target must be a scalar .binary value.
CANNOT_CAST_BINARY = Binary data cannot be converted to text without an explicit encoding.
CANNOT_EXPOSED_ARG = Procedure arguments cannot be exposed.
CANT_ASSIGN_IN_CLASS_DEF = Assignment is not allowed directly in a class definition.
CANT_ASSIGN_IN_INTERFACE_DEF = Assignment is not allowed directly in an interface definition.
CANT_DEFINE_CLASS_HERE = Class definitions are not allowed here.
CANT_DEFINE_INTERFACE_HERE = Interface definitions are not allowed here.
CANT_DEFINE_METHOD_HERE = Method definitions are not allowed here.
CANT_DEFINE_PROC_HERE = Procedure definitions are not allowed here.
CERTIFIED_EXIT_DISABLED = Certified compiler exit "{keyword}" is disabled.
CLASS_NOT_FOUND = Class was not found.
CONSTANT_REQUIRES_CONSTANT_EXPRESSION = Constant definitions require a constant expression.
DECIMAL_CASE_VALUE = NUMERIC CASE must be one of the supported case values.
DECIMAL_DIGITS_RANGE = NUMERIC DIGITS is outside the supported range.
DECIMAL_FORM_VALUE = NUMERIC FORM must be SCIENTIFIC or ENGINEERING.
DECIMAL_FUZZ_RANGE = NUMERIC FUZZ is outside the supported range.
DECIMAL_STANDARD_VALUE = NUMERIC STANDARD is not supported.
DEREFERENCE_REQUIRES_ASSIGNMENT = Dereference requires an assignment target.
DEREFERENCE_TARGET_NOT_LOCAL = Dereference target must be local storage.
DUPLICATE_NAMESPACE = Namespace is already declared.
DUPLICATE_SYMBOL = Symbol is already declared in this scope.
EXIT_BRIDGE_BAD_HELPER = Compiler exit helper has an invalid shape.
EXIT_BRIDGE_BAD_PLAN = Compiler exit returned an invalid rewrite plan.
EXIT_BRIDGE_BAD_RESULT = Compiler exit returned an invalid result.
EXIT_BRIDGE_DISPATCH_FAILED = Compiler exit dispatch failed.
EXIT_BRIDGE_ERROR = Compiler exit reported an error.
EXIT_BRIDGE_HELPER_BAD_SHAPE = Compiler exit helper {helper_id} has an invalid definition.
EXIT_BRIDGE_HELPER_CONFLICT = Compiler exit helper {helper_id} conflicts with an existing helper.
EXIT_BRIDGE_HELPER_CONTEXT_FAILED = Compiler exit helper {helper_id} could not create a context.
EXIT_BRIDGE_HELPER_INTERPOLATION_FAILED = Compiler exit helper {helper_id} could not be interpolated.
EXIT_BRIDGE_HELPER_MISSING_DEF = Compiler exit helper {helper_id} is missing its definition.
EXIT_BRIDGE_HELPER_MULTI_DEF = Compiler exit helper {helper_id} has more than one definition.
EXIT_BRIDGE_HELPER_PARSE_FAILED = Compiler exit helper {helper_id} could not be parsed.
EXIT_BRIDGE_HELPER_REGISTRY_FAILED = Compiler exit helper {helper_id} could not be registered.
EXIT_BRIDGE_PARSE_FAILED = Compiler exit result could not be parsed.
EXIT_BRIDGE_REPLACE_MISSING_TEXT = Compiler exit replacement is missing text.
EXIT_BRIDGE_UNSUPPORTED_HELPER_SCOPE = Compiler exit helper scope "{scope}" is not supported.
EXPECTING_ARRAY = Array value expected.
EXTERNAL_SHADOW_BYPASS = External symbol bypasses a shadowed declaration.
EXTRANEOUS_RETVAL = RETURN value is not expected here.
FACTORY_NOT_FOUND = Matching factory was not found.
IMPORTED_FUNCTION = Imported functions cannot be used in this context.
IMPLICIT_ADDRESS = Implicit ADDRESS command; quote command text or use ADDRESS explicitly.
INCOMPATIBLE_DIM_BASE = Array dimension {dim} has base {from}; expected {to}.
INCOMPATIBLE_DIM_SIZE = Array dimension {dim} has size {from}; expected {to}.
INCOMPATIBLE_OPTIONS = OPTIONS setting is incompatible with the current source level.
INTERFACE_DEFAULT_METHOD_REDEFINED = Class redefines default interface method {interface}.{member}.
INTERFACE_MATCH_SIGNATURE_MISMATCH = MATCH method for {interface}.{member} has an incompatible signature.
INTERFACE_MEMBER_BODY_NOT_ALLOWED = Interface members must not have a body here.
INTERFACE_MEMBER_NOT_IMPLEMENTED = Class does not implement interface member {interface}.{member}.
INTERFACE_MEMBER_SIGNATURE_MISMATCH = Implementation of {interface}.{member} has an incompatible signature.
INTERFACE_NOT_FOUND = Interface was not found.
INTERNAL_TEST = Internal test diagnostic.
INVALID_ASSEMBLER = Assembler text is invalid.
INVALID_BIN = Binary string is invalid.
INVALID_CONTROL_VARIABLE = Control variable is invalid for this loop.
INVALID_DO = DO instruction has an invalid combination of options.
INVALID_HEX = Hexadecimal string is invalid.
INVALID_LHS_ARRAY = Assignment target is not a valid array target.
INVALID_MAIN_ARGS = main must accept no arguments or a string array.
INVALID_PUBLIC_ATTRIBUTE = Public attribute access is invalid.
INVALID_REGISTER_ATTRIBUTE = Register attribute is invalid.
INVALID_REGISTER_FLAG_VIEW = Register flag view is invalid.
INVALID_SYMBOL_TYPE = Symbol has an invalid type for this context.
IS_A_CLASS = Symbol names a class, not a variable.
IS_A_FUNCTION = Symbol names a function, not a variable.
IS_A_NAMESPACE = Symbol names a namespace, not a variable.
LEAVE_WITH_REQUIRED = LEAVE in a block expression requires WITH.
LESS_THAN_BASE = Array bound is less than the base.
LOOP_CLASSES_NOT_SUPPORTED = Loop classes are not supported here.
MAIN_RETURNS_INTEGER = main must return an integer.
MATCH_WITHOUT_FACTORY = MATCH requires a corresponding factory.
METHOD_NOT_FOUND = Method was not found.
MISSING_VALUE = Value is required.
MISSING_END = Missing END for this construct.
MISSING_THEN = Missing THEN clause.
MULTIPLE_NAMESPACE = Only one namespace declaration is allowed.
NOT_AN_ARGUMENT = Symbol is not an argument.
NOT_AN_ARRAY = Value is not an array.
NOT_AN_OBJECT = Value is not an object.
NOT_IN_BLOCK_EXPR = Instruction is only valid inside a block expression.
NOT_IN_LOOP = Instruction is only valid inside a loop.
NOT_IN_SAME_SCOPE = Symbol is not in the same scope.
NUMERIC_CASE_NOT_FIRST_INST = NUMERIC CASE must precede executable instructions.
NUMERIC_DIGITS_NOT_FIRST_INST = NUMERIC DIGITS must precede executable instructions.
NUMERIC_FORM_NOT_FIRST_INST = NUMERIC FORM must precede executable instructions.
NUMERIC_FUZZ_NOT_FIRST_INST = NUMERIC FUZZ must precede executable instructions.
NUMERIC_STANDARD_NOT_FIRST_INST = NUMERIC STANDARD must precede executable instructions.
OUT_OF_MEMORY = Out of memory.
OUT_OF_RANGE = Value is outside the allowed range.
OVERFLOW_UNDERFLOW = Arithmetic overflow or underflow during optimisation.
PARSE_FAILURE = Source could not be parsed.
PROC_VAR_MISMATCH = Imported symbol "{name}" is a procedure/variable mismatch between {defining_file} and {import_file}.
READ_ONLY_REGISTER_FLAG_VIEW = Register flag view is read-only.
REFERENCE_TARGET_NOT_STORAGE = Reference target must be assignable storage.
REFERENCE_TYPE_MISMATCH = Reference type does not match.
REGISTER_FLAG_VIEW_REQUIRES_INT = Register flag view requires an integer register.
REGISTER_INDEX_OUT_OF_RANGE = Register index is outside the supported range.
REPEATED_ARG = ARG instruction is repeated.
REPEATED_NUMERIC_CASE = NUMERIC CASE is repeated.
REPEATED_NUMERIC_DIGITS = NUMERIC DIGITS is repeated.
REPEATED_NUMERIC_FORM = NUMERIC FORM is repeated.
REPEATED_NUMERIC_FUZZ = NUMERIC FUZZ is repeated.
REPEATED_NUMERIC_STANDARD = NUMERIC STANDARD is repeated.
RETURNS_VOID = Expression does not return a value.
RETVAL_MISSING = RETURN value is required.
RXC-LC-0 = Level C diagnostic.
RXC-LC-IMPLICIT_ADDRESS = Implicit ADDRESS command; quote command text or use ADDRESS explicitly.
RXPP_ALREADY_SOURCE_MAPPED = Input already contains options srcmap: {file}.
RXPP_ALREADY_SOURCE_MAPPED_HINT = Run rxc on generated source-map output; do not run rxpp twice.
RXPP_EXPANSION_LIMIT = Maximum macro expansion limit exceeded after {count}.
RXPP_FILE_TERMINATED = RXPP processing of {file} terminated.
RXPP_INCLUDE_MISSING = Include file is missing: {file}.
RXPP_MACLIB_MISSING = Macro library was not found or is not accessible: {file}.
RXPP_MACRO_EMPTY_BODY = Macro body is empty or missing braces: {name}.
RXPP_MACRO_MISSING_RPAREN = Macro definition is missing a closing parenthesis: {definition}.
RXPP_MACRO_UNCLOSED = Macro definition is not closed: {name}.
RXPP_MISSING_ENDIF = No matching ##ENDIF found after line {line}.
RXPP_NO_SOURCE_FILE = No source file was specified.
RXPP_POSITIONAL_AFTER_KEYWORD = Positional parameter follows keyword parameter in {macro}({arguments}).
RXPP_SCRIPT_MACRO_MISSING = Script macro file was not found: {file}.
RXPP_SOURCE_MISSING = Source file is missing: {file}.
RXPP_SYSTEM_MACLIB_MISSING = System macro library was not found or is not accessible: {file}.
RXPP_TERMINATED = RXPP processing terminated.
SHADOWING = Symbol shadows an earlier declaration.
SIGNAL_BLOCK_ONLY_LEVELB = SIGNAL block syntax is only supported in Level B.
SIGNAL_CANNOT_BE_MASKED = This signal cannot be masked.
SRCMAP_MALFORMED = Source map directive is malformed: {reason}.
SRCMAP_UNBALANCED = Source map span is not balanced: {reason}.
SYMBOL_HAS_BOUNDARY_WHITESPACE = Symbol has invalid boundary whitespace.
SYNC_TEST = Source synchronisation test diagnostic.
SYNTAX_ERROR = Syntax error.
TAKENCONSTANT_ARRAY = TAKENCONSTANT cannot be applied to an array target.
TYPE_MISMATCH = Type mismatch.
UNEXPECTED_ARGUMENT = Unexpected argument at position {position}.
UNEXPECTED_ARRAY = Scalar value expected, but an array was provided.
UNEXPECTED_ELSE = Unexpected ELSE.
UNEXPECTED_END = Unexpected END.
UNEXPECTED_OTHERWISE = Unexpected OTHERWISE.
UNEXPECTED_THEN = Unexpected THEN.
UNEXPECTED_WHEN = Unexpected WHEN.
UNEXPECTED_VALUE = Value is not expected here.
UNKNOWN_SIGNAL_NAME = Signal name is not known.
UNKNOWN_SYMBOL = Symbol was not found.
UNKNOWN_TYPE = Type was not found.
UNUSED_IMPORT = Import is recognised but not used.
UPDATING_TAKEN_CONSTANT = Taken constant cannot be updated.
INCOMPLETE_DO = Incomplete DO instruction.
INVALID_EXPRESSION = Invalid expression.

